    "raw_answer": "To find the relative direction of the refrigerator from your position at the washer when facing the stove, we can analyze their coordinates on the top-view grid:\n\n* **Washer (Your Position):** $[4.5, 1.5]$\n* **Stove (Facing Direction):** $[5.5, 6.5]$\n* **Refrigerator (Target):** $[2.5, 4.5]$\n\n1. **Determine the facing vector (from Washer to Stove):**\n   $$\\vec{v}_{\\text{facing}} = [5.5 - 4.5, 6.5 - 1.5] = [1.0, 5.0]$$\n   This vector points mostly \"up\" (North) and slightly \"right\" (East).\n\n2. **Determine the target vector (from Washer to Refrigerator):**\n   $$\\vec{v}_{\\text{target}} = [2.5 - 4.5, 4.5 - 1.5] = [-2.0, 3.0]$$\n   This vector points \"left\" (West) and \"up\" (North).\n\n3. **Calculate the relative position:**\n   * **Forward/Backward component:** The dot product of the target vector and the facing vector is:\n     $$[1.0, 5.0] \\cdot [-2.0, 3.0] = (1.0 \\times -2.0) + (5.0 \\times 3.0) = -2.0 + 15.0 = 13.0$$\n     Since this is positive, the refrigerator is in **front** of you.\n   * **Left/Right component:** The 2D cross product (or determinant) of the facing vector and the target vector determines if it is to the left or right:\n     $$x_1 y_2 - y_1 x_2 = (1.0 \\times 3.0) - (5.0 \\times -2.0) = 3.0 - (-10.0) = 13.0$$\n     Since this is positive, the target is to your **left**.\n\nThus, the refrigerator is to your **front-left**.\n\nANSWER: B",
